<p>NOTE: (a) 1997 earnings include (1) a one-time non-cash stock option charge of $22.5 million related to the conversion of stock options at the time of the initial public offering, (2) an income tax benefit of $23.2 million reflecting the recoverability of a portion of the net operating loss carryforward, and (3) a charge of $0.7 million for the write-off of unamortized debt financing associated with the redemption of the 13-1/4% discount debentures. (b) The decrease in weighted average shares in 1997 resulted from the repurchase of approximately 4.3 million shares in July 1996, net of shares issued in February 1997 in conjunction with the initial public offering.  If the initial public offering had occured as of January 1, 1997, the weighted average shares in the first quarter would have been 20.5 million.</p>
